   </div></details></nav></div></header><script>(function(){var d=document.querySelector(".mnav");if(!d)return;document.addEventListener("click",function(e){if(d.open&&!d.contains(e.target))d.open=false});document.addEventListener("keydown",function(e){if(e.key==="Escape"&&d.open){d.open=false;d.querySelector("summary").focus()}})})();</script><main><nav class="crumb w" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <span>NCLEX test-day simulation</span></nav><section class="hero w"><h1>Rehearse NCLEX Test Day, Before Test Day</h1><p class="lead">Test-day mode turns the adaptive exam into a proctored rehearsal: a locked screen, webcam checks, a 5-hour clock that keeps running on breaks, no going back, and an integrity report when you finish. Nothing on exam day should be a surprise.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#start/testday">Start a proctored practice exam</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools">For nursing programs</a></div></section><div class="w"><h2>Why rehearse the conditions, not just the questions</h2><p>Most NCLEX practice happens on a couch with a phone nearby, the freedom to pause, and the option to go back. Test day is different: your belongings are in a locker, the clock never stops, every answer is final, and someone is watching. Practicing under those conditions at least once means the room, the rules, and the clock feel familiar, so your attention goes to the questions.</p>
       <h2>Test day vs. test-day mode</h2><div class="tw"><table class="cmp"><thead><tr><th></th><th>At the NCLEX testing center</th><th>In Vexcura test-day mode</th></tr></thead><tbody>
       <tr><td><b>Check-in</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">Photo, signature, and palm vein scan, then you sign the candidate statement.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">You agree to the candidate rules and take a check-in photo with a face check. Your name is watermarked on the screen.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Your belongings</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">Phones and devices go in a sealed bag in a locker. Watches, notes, food, and drinks stay outside the room.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">You confirm no phones, smartwatches, notes, or other devices are within reach. Screenshot keys and shortcuts are blocked and logged.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Monitoring</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">You test in a monitored room, and irregular behavior is reported.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">Optional webcam checks flag a covered camera, no face, a second person, or looking away for too long. Every time you leave the window is recorded.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>The clock</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">5 hours total, including breaks. The clock doesn't stop.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">The same 5-hour clock, and it keeps running on breaks.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Breaks</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">Optional breaks are offered after about 2 hours and again after about 3½ hours.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">Take breaks the same way, on a running clock, so you can practice your timing.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Answers</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">Once you submit an answer, you can't go back.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">The same. Every answer is final.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Tools</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">An on-screen calculator and an erasable note board.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">An on-screen calculator on every item. Keep one blank sheet or a small whiteboard as your note board.</td></tr>
       <tr><td><b>Breaking the rules</b></td><td data-l="At the testing center">Results can be withheld or canceled.</td><td data-l="In test-day mode">Irregularities are logged, and you can choose to have the exam end automatically after repeated irregularities.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
       <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Testing-center rules summarized from the NCSBN NCLEX candidate rules and exam-day information at nclex.com. Always check nclex.com for the current rules before your appointment.</p>
       <figure class="shot"><div class="dv dv-b"><div class="dv-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span><svg viewBox="0 0 12 14" width="9" height="11" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 6V4.2a3 3 0 0 1 6 0V6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6"/><rect x="1.5" y="6" width="9" height="7" rx="1.6" fill="currentColor"/></svg>vexcura.com</span></div><div class="dv-v"><img src="/img/exam-q-1000.webp" srcset="/img/exam-q-1600.webp 1600w, /img/exam-q-1000.webp 1000w" sizes="(max-width: 760px) calc(100vw - 32px), 720px" width="1000" height="625" alt="The full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam in progress: item 5 with the five-hour timer, calculator and an answer selected" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></div></div><figcaption>Test-day mode proctors the same full adaptive exam: 85 to 150 items on a five-hour clock.</figcaption></figure>
       <h2>Your integrity report</h2><div class="feat"><div><b>Status at a glance</b>Clean, Minor flags, or Irregular, so you know whether you held test-day discipline.</div><div><b>Time-stamped log</b>Every event, from leaving the window to looking away, at the moment it happened.</div><div><b>Breaks and timing</b>How many breaks you took and how much of the 5 hours you used.</div><div><b>PDF download</b>Keep it with your results or share it with an instructor.</div></div>
       <h2>Planning to test at home?</h2><p>NCSBN is developing NCLEX Online, an at-home version of the exam with live proctors and a room scan. Choose <b>At home</b> in test-day mode to rehearse those steps now. <a href="/nclex-at-home">What we know about taking the NCLEX at home</a>.</p>
       <h2>For nursing programs</h2><p>Faculty can ask students to complete a proctored practice exam before graduation and review the results and integrity reports together. It's a simple way to see who is ready for test-day conditions, not just test-day content. <a href="/about">Learn about Vexcura</a>.</p>
       <h2>Run a full rehearsal</h2><ol><li>Block 5 uninterrupted hours, ideally at the same time of day as your NCLEX appointment.</li><li>Use a laptop or desktop in a quiet room. Put your phone in another room and clear the desk except for one blank sheet.</li><li>Start the full exam with test-day mode on, and turn on the webcam if you have one.</li><li>Take your breaks at about 2 hours and 3½ hours, and notice how long they really take on a running clock.</li><li>Afterward, review your category scores and your integrity report. Fix one habit before the next rehearsal.</li></ol>
       <div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/#start/testday">Start a proctored practice exam</a></div>
       <h2>Common questions</h2><h3>Is this an official proctored NCLEX exam?</h3><p>No. Vexcura is an independent practice tool. Test-day mode recreates the conditions of the real exam so you can rehearse them, but it is not run, scored, or recognized by NCSBN or Pearson VUE.</p><h3>Does the webcam record or upload video?</h3><p>No. Webcam checks run entirely on your own device. No video or images are uploaded or stored, and your check-in photo is discarded when you leave the results page.</p><h3>Do I need a webcam?</h3><p>No. You can take a test-day exam without a camera. Fullscreen, focus tracking, breaks, and the integrity report still work.</p><h3>What does the integrity report show?</h3><p>A status of Clean, Minor flags, or Irregular, a session ID, the name you typed for the watermark, time used, breaks taken, and a time-stamped list of every event, such as leaving the window or another person appearing on camera. You can download it as a PDF.</p><h3>Can my instructor see my integrity report?</h3><p>If you take the exam while signed in to your Vexcura account, site administrators can see your integrity reports along with your exam summaries. Schools that use Vexcura with their students can use these reports to review practice under test-day conditions.</p><h3>What device should I use?</h3><p>A laptop or desktop computer, like the one you'll use at the testing center. Phones and some tablets don't support locked fullscreen.</p><h3>Can I rehearse the at-home NCLEX?</h3><p>Yes. Choose &quot;At home&quot; in test-day mode to add a room scan and workspace checks modeled on NCSBN's planned NCLEX Online. NCSBN hasn't set a launch date and says it isn't coming in 2026, so the preview will be updated as details are released.</p><h3>How do I get test-day mode?</h3><p>It's included with the adaptive exam, which students get free through their nursing program's license.</p>
       <p class="src" style="color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px">Webcam checks run on your device. No video or images are uploaded or stored. Vexcura's integrity report is a practice record, not a Pearson VUE or NCSBN record.</p><h2>Related</h2><ul class="rel"><li><a href="/free-nclex-practice-exam">Full adaptive NCLEX-RN practice exam</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-pass-guarantee">NCLEX pass guarantee: registration fee back if you qualify and don't pass</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-at-home">Can you take the NCLEX at home?</a></li><li><a href="/next-generation-nclex">Next Generation NCLEX (NGN) guide</a></li><li><a href="/nclex-study-guides">Free NCLEX study guides (PDF)</a></li></ul></div><section class="band vxs-band"><div class="vxs-bg" data-vxs-i="0" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="vxs-sh" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="w"><h2>Bring Vexcura to your nursing program</h2><p>1,220 cited NCLEX-RN questions, adaptive practice exams, 8 NGN case studies, an Epic-style academic EHR and a clinical instructor workspace. The school pays; students and instructors are always free, and every plan includes everything. Students: ask your instructor, or join with your school's code.</p><div class="cta"><a class="btn" href="/for-nursing-schools">See Vexcura for nursing schools</a><a class="btn alt" href="/for-nursing-schools#pricing">Pricing</a><a class="btn alt" href="/#signup">Join with a school code</a></div></div></section></main><footer class="foot mktf"><div class="w">
